wip/materialx: Import materialx-1.39.5

MaterialX is an open standard for exchanging material and look
development content; OpenUSD and Blender use it.  Shared C++
libraries, the data library, GLSL/MSL/OSL/MDL/Slang shader
generators, the GLSL and Metal render modules (MSL is compiled at run
time through the Metal API), OpenImageIO support and PyMaterialX.

The data library goes to share/MaterialX/libraries, with a fallback
search path patched into the C++ library and a link from the Python
package.  The viewer and graph editor need git submodules that are not
in the release tarball, so they are not built.
